    "created_at": "2023-08-25T15:27:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-08-25T15:27:40Z",
    "body": ">I think ensuring that the end user knows what ends up being shared is important. \r\n\r\nAgreed! I think that was the original reasoning for the addition to the W3C spec, and I like the wording that they had there\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/w3c/html/pull/1372/files\r\n\r\n>When fields with the <{autocompleteelements/autocomplete}> attribute wearing the <a>autofill expectation mantle</a> are hidden off-screen or visually disguised, personal data may still be entered when using the autofill feature of browsers and password managers. User agents should verify that all fields with the <{autocompleteelements/autocomplete}> attribute wearing the <a>autofill expectation mantle</a> are visible within the viewport before automatically entering data.",
